    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Several identical pipes can be counted from the net rate.\n\nSuppose 10 pipes are open. Each inlet fills in 10 h; each waste pipe empties in 30 h. The tank fills in 3 h.\nLet x be inlets, so 10−x are waste pipes.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "x/10 − (10−x)/30 = 1/3.\nMultiply by 30:\n3x − (10−x) = 10\n4x = 20 → x = 5.\nSo 5 are waste pipes too.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
